Huge milestone for an incredible team I’ve been fortunate to support. Fast, efficient inference is a key infrastructure challenge in AI. Excited to see Etched push the frontier here, and about what this could unlock for diffusion LLMs.

Congrats to the team on coming out of stealth.

@Etched: "We're coming out of stealth. We've built our first racks after a successful A0 tapeout, over $1 billion in customer contracts, and $800 million raised. Early customer tests show us achieving state-of-the-art throughput, latency, and power efficiency on inference workloads. Our first racks ship this summer."

Interesting failure mode: turning web search off improved a model’s WideSearch score.

@apoorv_umang: "We turned web search off and one model’s WideSearch score went up. WideSearch is a benchmark for agentic search. Every model gains from retrieval: Haiku +0.19, Mercury +0.13, except Gemini: −0.02."

Backstory: Mercury did worse than Gemini on WideSearch. A customer asked why. So we dug in.

🚀 v3 is out! The Principles of Diffusion Models on arXiv has been updated ahead of its MIT Press publication in 2027.

The new version features a 'Road Ahead' chapter on discrete diffusion, major restructuring including a diffusion solvers chapter, and reader guides for each chapter. With continuous diffusion for language making a comeback, many principles in the book can carry over. Check out the new version via the link in the thread.

@JCJesseLai highlights that the monograph provides a systematic and fundamental recipe to understand diffusion modeling, explaining how current models work, why they work, and future directions. The authors invite feedback and discussions, with a forthcoming markdown version for comments.
